USB gadget f_rndis: make CDC call-management bDataInterface dynamic.

Upstream-Status: Pending

f_rndis hardcodes its CDC Call Management descriptor's bDataInterface at
0x01. That is only correct when the RNDIS control/data interfaces land at
0/1. In a composite where another function (here: AMI's HID at interface
0, to match eth_mod.c's device shape) is linked first, RNDIS lands at
1/2 and the hardcoded pointer dangles: it points back at the control
interface instead of the data interface, the CDC chain becomes invalid,
and strictly-parsing hosts (Windows usbccgp, AMI's BIOS USB-NIC driver)
discard the whole configuration and disable the port, even though every
enumeration stage succeeded.

Patch bDataInterface at bind time to the actual data interface id, the
same way the union descriptor's master/slave pointers are already
patched. The static is zero-initialised instead of hardcoded, so the
behaviour for the plain single-function layout is identical (control=0,
data=1 assigned at bind) while a composite gets the correct pointer.

Note: the descriptor static is shared across multiple f_rndis instances,
so the value always reflects the last-bound instance -- the same
limitation already present for the patched union descriptor fields.

Signed-off-by: OpenBMC bring-up (Gigabyte MC12-LE0 port)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_rndis.c
@@ -124,7 +124,9 @@
 	.bDescriptorSubType =	USB_CDC_CALL_MANAGEMENT_TYPE,
 
 	.bmCapabilities =	0x00,
-	.bDataInterface =	0x01,
+	/* .bDataInterface patched in rndis_bind(): must be the data
+	 * interface of THIS instance, not a hardcoded 0x01 (which is
+	 * only right when f_rndis is the first composite function). */
 };
 
 static struct usb_cdc_acm_descriptor rndis_acm_descriptor = {
@@ -722,6 +724,13 @@
 
 	rndis_data_intf.bInterfaceNumber = status;
 	rndis_union_desc.bSlaveInterface0 = status;
+	/*
+	 * CDC Call Management: point at THIS instance's data interface.
+	 * The upstream hardcoded 0x01 is wrong when f_rndis is not the
+	 * first composite function (e.g. AMI-style HID at interface 0
+	 * shifts RNDIS control/data to 1/2).
+	 */
+	call_mgmt_descriptor.bDataInterface = status;
 
 	/* allocate instance-specific endpoints */
 	ep = usb_ep_autoconfig(cdev->gadget, &fs_in_desc);
